<resources>
    <!-- No ambient display: the 9900's screen stays dark when locked, a new
         message lights its LED and nothing else (user guide 7.1, p. 15, B; docs/BBOS7-VISUEL.md
         §5 and §10). Android, through SystemUI's DozeService (set by BenOS's overlays, read on
         the Q25 by dumpsys dreams), lit the screen with its clock and the card of each new
         notification (pulse, doze_enabled on by default, config_pulseOnNotificationsAvailable).
         Empty is AOSP's own value for a device without ambient display: AmbientDisplayConfiguration
         then says it is unavailable, DreamManagerService starts no doze dream, and the screen goes
         from on to off (PowerManagerService's path when no dream runs). Nothing of the lock
         itself depends on it. -->
    <string name="config_dozeComponent" translatable="false"></string>
</resources>
